# Build output.
#
# The native libraries used to be TRACKED here, on the reasoning that CI
# checked out a tree with no core in it and produced an app that installs,
# starts, and cannot run a single game -- with nothing in the pipeline
# noticing, because a missing core is not a build error.
#
# That reasoning no longer holds. The core is a submodule of this repository,
# so any checkout can build it, android/build-core.sh installs its output
# straight into the directory Gradle packages, and it refuses to run at all
# when the submodule has not been initialised. Committing 40 MB of binaries per
# ABI to work around a problem that no longer exists is not a trade worth
# making.
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/
android/app/libs/
android/build/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
**/build/
*.iml
.gradle/

# Build outputs are never committed.
dist/
*.apk
*.aab

# Keystores. The upload keystore is registered with Play Console; never commit
# it.
*.jks
*.keystore

# DOS games and disc images are never committed.
*.iso
*.cue
*.ima
*.vhd

# ...except the bundled demo content, which is an app ASSET rather than
# somebody's game: FreeDOS is what lets the emulator boot a real DOS with
# nothing supplied by the user, and it has to be in the repository for a cloud
# build to bundle it. Unmodified and freely redistributable; provenance and
# licence in demo/NOTICE.md.
!android/app/src/main/assets/demo/FREEDOS.IMG
!android/app/src/main/assets/demo/DEMO.COM

.DS_Store

# Signing config for a developer machine; never committed.
key.properties
android/key.properties

# iOS build output (SDL3, the configured engine tree, the static libs).
ios/build/

__pycache__/

# The signing passphrase is NEVER committed; only the encrypted blobs are.
ios/signing/*.passphrase
ios/signing/*.decrypted
.kotlin/
